Content-Disposition: form-data; name="explanation"

This is the source-faithful two-step analytic reduction. The first Open child is the original theorem that the analytic remainder tends to zero. The second Open child is the original selected-minor logarithmic bound. The unchanged six-line source proof combines them to establish the existing analytic aggregate interface. Both children remain Open, so this verification is a SKETCH_ACCEPTED decomposition rather than a closed proof.
